  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(59.16pt, 210.38pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.264pt, 210.38pt, "—In this work, we experimentally investigate the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 221.54pt, "gradient stress (σ₁) in 128° Y-cut transferred thin film lithium ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 232.34pt, "niobate (TFLN) films with thicknesses from 100 to 460 nm using ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 243.26pt, "cantilever curvature analysis. The results reveal a strong ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 254.21pt, "dependence of σ₁ on both crystallographic orientation and film ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 265.01pt, "thickness, with stress-free orientations at ~55° and ~125° for 220–")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 275.93pt, "460 nm films, shifting to ~20° and ~160° for 100 nm films. The ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 286.73pt, "extracted normalized σ₁ ranges from −0.1 to 3.4 MPa/nm (100 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 297.65pt, "nm), −0.8 to 0.34 MPa/nm (220 nm), and −0.12 to 0.08 MPa/nm ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 308.45pt, "(460 nm), indicating a pronounced thickness-dependent through-")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 319.37pt, "thickness stress gradient. Finite element simulations show ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 330.17pt, "excellent agreement with the measurements, validating the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 341.09pt, "curvature-based extraction method and confirming that σ₁ ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 352.01pt, "originates from ")
  #line-at(122.823pt, 352.01pt, "an orientation-dependent ")
  #line-at(236.861pt, 352.01pt, "residual ")
  #line-at(277.388pt, 352.01pt, "stress ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 362.81pt, "gradient. To mitigate this effect, a bilayer TFLN structure with ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 373.73pt, "opposite crystallographic orientations, forming a periodically ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 384.53pt, "poled piezoelectric film (P3F), is investigated, enabling partial ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 395.45pt, "cancellation of σ₁. A 90/110 nm P3F bilayer reduces the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 406.25pt, "equivalent normalized σ₁ to −0.4 to −0.04 MPa/nm, resulting in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 417.17pt, "significantly reduced deformation. These results establish ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 427.99pt, "gradient stress engineering through orientation, thickness, and ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 438.91pt, "bilayer design as an effective strategy for achieving mechanically ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 449.83pt, "stable and scalable TFLN microelectromechanical systems ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 460.63pt, "(MEMS) devices.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.8pt, 482.71pt, "Index Terms")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(94.584pt, 482.71pt, "— Thin film lithium niobate (TFLN), residual stress ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 493.03pt, "anisotropy, gradient stress, periodically poled piezoelectric film ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 503.47pt, "(P3F) ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(131.06pt, 526.75pt, "I.")
  #line-at(138.98pt, 526.75pt, "INTRODUCTION ")
  #line-at(79.224pt, 542.23pt, "ESIDUAL stress plays a critical role in the mechanical ")
  #line-at(79.224pt, 554.35pt, "reliability and performance of thin-film micro- and ")
  #line-at(79.224pt, 566.35pt, "nano-electromechanical systems (MEMS and NEMS), ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 578.47pt, "radio frequency (RF) devices, and optical components. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 590.59pt, "Excessive residual stress can lead to structural deformation ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 602.62pt, "and failure of suspended structures during release, resulting in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 614.74pt, "break, collapse, or buckling, as illustrated in Fig. 1. More ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 626.74pt, "generally, residual stress in thin-film systems can give rise to ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 638.86pt, "various mechanical instabilities and structural failures. Tensile ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 662.26pt, "This work was supported by the DARPA Chemistries and monoLayers for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 671.86pt, "Anti-aging Kinematics (CLOAK) program and by a fellowship from the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 681.58pt, "Ministry ")
  #line-at(85.649pt, 681.58pt, "of ")
  #line-at(103.747pt, 681.58pt, "National ")
  #line-at(142.597pt, 681.58pt, "Defense ")
  #line-at(180.007pt, 681.58pt, "of ")
  #line-at(197.984pt, 681.58pt, "the ")
  #line-at(218.969pt, 681.58pt, "Republic ")
  #line-at(259.145pt, 681.58pt, "of ")
  #line-at(277.122pt, 681.58pt, "Korea. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 691.18pt, "Any opinions, findings, conclusions, or recommendations expressed in this ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 700.896pt, "material are those of the author(s) and do not necessarily reflect the views of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 710.496pt, "the Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency (DARPA). ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 720.216pt, "The authors are with the Electrical and Computer Engineering Department, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 729.816pt, "University of Texas at Austin, Austin, TX 78712 USA (e-mail: ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 739.536pt, "c18263@utexas.edu)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.25pt, 210.74pt, "residual stress often results in film cracking [1], [2], while ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 222.86pt, "compressive stress can induce delamination, buckling, or ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 234.98pt, "blistering of multilayer stacks [3], [4], [5]. Beyond mechanical ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 246.98pt, "failure, residual stress distributions can influence adhesion, ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 259.13pt, "fracture toughness [6], and the resonant behavior of ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 271.13pt, "microstructures [7]. At the same time, controlled stress has ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 283.25pt, "been intentionally utilized as a design parameter to enhance ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 295.37pt, "device functionality. Engineered stress has been shown to ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 307.37pt, "improve electrical conductivity [8], modify dielectric ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 319.49pt, "permittivity [9], enhance piezoelectric response [10], tailor ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 331.61pt, "magnetic anisotropy [11], and improve acoustic resonator ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 343.61pt, "performance [12]. These examples highlight that residual ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 355.73pt, "stress is not merely an unwanted byproduct of fabrication but ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 367.73pt, "a physical parameter that can be harnessed to optimize device ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 379.85pt, "performance. ")
  #line-at(323.33pt, 391.97pt, "Lithium niobate (LN) is a widely used piezoelectric and ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 403.97pt, "electro-optic material with strong elastic anisotropy and ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 416.09pt, "electromechanical coupling. In recent years, transferred thin-")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 428.11pt, "film lithium niobate (TFLN) has emerged as an enabling ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 440.23pt, "platform for next-generation microsystems due to its ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 452.35pt, "compatibility ")
  #line-at(378.11pt, 452.35pt, "with ")
  #line-at(407.372pt, 452.35pt, "nanofabrication ")
  #line-at(481.564pt, 452.35pt, "and ")
  #line-at(507.47pt, 452.35pt, "heterogeneous ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 464.35pt, "integration. Suspended structures fabricated in TFLN have ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 476.47pt, "enabled a wide range of devices including RF resonators [13], ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 488.59pt, "filters [14], photonic circuits [15], [16], and piezoelectric ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 500.59pt, "MEMS based sensors [17]. In addition, cantilever-type ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 512.71pt, "piezoelectric structures have been explored for sensing ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 524.71pt, "applications [18]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#d13438"))
  #line-at(383.47pt, 524.71pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(385.99pt, 524.71pt, " piezoelectric energy harvesting [19], and ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 536.83pt, "optical beam steering [20],where the mechanical stability and ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 548.95pt, "curvature of suspended beams directly influence device ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 560.95pt, "performance.  ")
  #line-at(323.33pt, 573.07pt, "Residual stress in TFLN has been investigated in several ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 585.07pt, "contexts. Previous studies have primarily focused on the mean ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 597.34pt, "residual stress (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(380.95pt, 597.34pt, "𝜎")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(386.11pt, 599.38pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(390.55pt, 597.34pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(396.07pt, 597.34pt, " in LN thin films rather than its spatial ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 609.7pt, "distribution. In epitaxial LN films, ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(464.35pt, 609.7pt, "𝜎")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(469.51pt, 611.74pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(475.63pt, 609.7pt, " arises from substrate ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 621.82pt, "clamping during cooling, which constrains the in-plane thermal ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 633.94pt, "expansion of the film and produces biaxial in-plane stress [21]. ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 645.94pt, "Similar stress has been reported in bonded LN/Si hybrid wafers ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 658.06pt, "due to the thermal expansion mismatch between LN and silicon ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 670.18pt, "during bonding and annealing [22]. Various approaches have ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 682.18pt, "been explored to mitigate this mean stress, including wafer ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 694.296pt, "thickness optimization [21], wafer-bow engineering [23], and ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 706.416pt, "low-temperature bonding processes [22]. Despite these efforts, ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 718.416pt, "residual stress is typically treated as a uniform in-plane stress ")
  #line-at(313.25pt, 730.536pt, "averaged across the film thickness.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 48.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.8pt, 566.47pt, "R")
]

