#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 514.5pt), 47pt, 54pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(560.26pt, 30.96pt, "4 ")
  #line-at(138.14pt, 259.01pt, "III.")
  #line-at(152.78pt, 259.01pt, "F")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(158.3pt, 259.01pt, "ABRICATION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 274.49pt, "Micromachined cantilever arrays were fabricated from 128° ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 286.49pt, "Y-cut TFLN on Si substrates provided by NGK Corporation. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 298.61pt, "In addition to single-layer films with thicknesses of 100 nm, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 310.73pt, "220 nm, and 460 nm, a bilayer stack was investigated to ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 322.73pt, "examine the effect of multilayer structures on residual stress ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 334.85pt, "behavior. The bilayer is based on a P3F configuration with ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 346.85pt, "opposite crystallographic orientations in the two layers, which ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 358.97pt, "ideally enables symmetric stress compensation. In this work, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 371.09pt, "the bilayer consists of 90 nm (top) and 110 nm (bottom) LN ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 383.09pt, "layers, reflecting slight thickness variation in the as-fabricated ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 395.21pt, "stack. The crystallographic configurations of both single-layer ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 407.33pt, "and bilayer structures are illustrated in Fig. 3(a). ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 419.33pt, "Each cantilever set consisted of beams with in-plane ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 431.47pt, "orientations ranging from θ = 0° to 160° in 20° increments, as ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 443.47pt, "shown in Fig. 3(b). To achieve finer angular resolution, four ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 455.59pt, "identical sets were patterned with a 5° rotation offset between ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 467.71pt, "them, resulting in a combined array spanning θ = 0° to 175° in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 479.71pt, "5° increments (36 orientation groups per film thickness). This ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 491.83pt, "layout enables systematic mapping of orientation-dependent ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 503.83pt, "stress behavior across the wafer. Representative released ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 515.95pt, "cantilevers at different orientations are shown in the SEM ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 528.07pt, "image in Fig. 3(c), illustrating the strong orientation ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 540.07pt, "dependence of the beam curvature. ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 552.19pt, "The fabrication process is summarized in Fig. 3(d). First, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 564.31pt, "the cantilever patterns were defined using maskless ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 576.31pt, "photolithography. Following lithography, a chromium (Cr) ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 588.43pt, "layer was deposited by electron-beam evaporation to serve as ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 600.46pt, "a hard mask for subsequent dry etching. A lift-off process was ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 612.58pt, "then performed to define the Cr etch mask, leaving Cr only in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 624.7pt, "the desired cantilever regions. Using this Cr hard mask, the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 636.7pt, "exposed 128° Y-cut LN layer was etched by inductively ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 648.82pt, "coupled plasma reactive ion etching (ICP-RIE). A low-")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 660.82pt, "temperature ICP-RIE process was employed to minimize ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 672.94pt, "additional thermal residual stress during etching. After LN ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 685.06pt, "patterning, the Cr hard mask was removed using a selective Cr ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 697.056pt, "wet etchant, ensuring that no residual masking material ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 709.176pt, "remained on the device surface. Finally, the suspended ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 721.296pt, "cantilever structures were released by isotropic silicon etching ")
